# Type-safe, lint-clean code

This project uses `strict: true` TypeScript and `next build` runs type checking. Do not ship code that fails `npm run build` or `npm run lint`.

- Match React 18 DOM types: boolean attributes like `inert` must be `boolean`, not strings (`inert` or `inert={true}`, never `{...{ inert: '' }}`).
- Do not use type assertions or `any` to silence errors unless the types are genuinely wrong and there is no cleaner fix.
- After editing `.ts` / `.tsx` files, check lints and fix new errors before finishing.
- Prefer explicit types that compile under `strict` (no implicit `any`, correct prop types, valid JSX).
